    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0119" n="37" xml:id="pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d59-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-16">16 January 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 167, Top Secret and Personal, for Ambassador Harriman from the President.</p>
                <p>Referring to Deane’s M22351<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d59-f2"/> of 14 January and your . . . [telegram of January
                        16].<anchor n="3" xml:id="d59-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>I hope that you will be able to arrange, without offending the Russians, for the
                    setting up of my personal mess ashore and the use of my stewards and cooks. I
                    desire this in order to maintain my usual diet. Our supplies will be obtained
                    from the <hi rendition="#italic">Catoctin</hi>.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d59-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d59-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d59-f2" n="2" xml:id="d59-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d59-f3" n="3" xml:id="d59-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
